// The mic must not be able to stay grey.
//
// Re-arming after speech depends on a chain: audio.onended -> finishTTSPlayback
// -> ttsTick -> the queue drains -> resumeSttAfterSpeech. Every link has broken
// at least once, and each break was fixed where it broke: the duck with no undo
// on the element path, the hard-skip that bypassed ttsTick, browser TTS that
// never fired onend because no voice matched the language, the auto-voice
// timeout above. Four fixes, one symptom — a mic that goes grey and stays grey.
//
// So this does not add a fifth link. It states the invariant and repairs it:
// voice mode on, nothing playing, recogniser idle is a state that should not
// persist, whatever broke upstream. Two consecutive ticks before acting, so a
// legitimate gap between utterances is not mistaken for the fault.
//
// It matters most where nobody can reach the mic button. This was reported from
// an Android TV, where the recovery for a grey mic is a remote control and a
// pointer that does not exist.
// Two states are covered, because the parking above created the second one.
// resumeSttAfterSpeech() is reached from ttsTick()'s empty-queue branch, so a
// greeting that finishes without passing through ttsTick -- the browser
// speechSynthesis fallback has done exactly that -- would leave
// autoVoicePending set and never honoured, and the invariant tick would not see
// it either, because voice mode was never entered. Handing the timeout's intent
// to one call site made that call site load-bearing; this is the backstop for it.
