// means "waiting for the model" needs: "routing…" expired after a second while
// the request was still in flight, so anyone listening to this region heard the
// question acknowledged and then nothing for as long as the model took. The
// reply path already calls showStage("") when the first token lands, so the
// hold has a real end rather than a guessed duration.
//
// Two bounds on the hold. At STAGE_SLOW_MS the label says so, because silence
// and slowness are indistinguishable otherwise. At STAGE_MAX_MS it clears
// regardless — a request that dies without reaching any clear path should not
// leave a stale "routing…" sitting in a live region forever.
